# exec-update settings.  cp exec-update.env.example exec-update.env  and edit.
#
# The real exec-update.env is gitignored - it describes THIS controller's
# layout, which differs per machine.
#
# An exported variable beats this file, so a one-off override still works:
#   REMOTE_BIN_REL=some/other/path ./update-exec.sh my-branch --all
#
# "~/" is expanded to your home directory. Values are literal otherwise -
# no $VAR substitution.


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CONTROLLER SIDE - put these wherever you like
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# git checkout of rubixgoplatform used to BUILD. Only the controller needs it;
# the fleet nodes never see source code.
#
# Do NOT put this inside ~/Desktop/rubix - a FILE named "rubixgoplatform"
# already lives there (the running binary), so a clone of the same name
# collides. Anywhere else is fine.
REPO_DIR=~/Desktop/rubixgoplatform

# Optional: skip the build and ship a binary produced elsewhere. Useful when
# the controller has no Go toolchain. Must be a LINUX (ELF) binary - the
# Makefile sets CGO_ENABLED=1, so it cannot be cross-compiled from Windows or
# macOS without a C toolchain. Leave commented out for the normal build path.
# PREBUILT_BINARY=/tmp/rubixgoplatform-fix


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TARGET SIDE - this one is NOT free to choose
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Where the binary lives on each NODE, relative to that node's $HOME.
#
# It must match what the node's systemd unit actually runs. On this fleet:
#   ExecStart=$HOME/Desktop/rubix/rubixgoplatform run -p $HOME/Desktop/rubix/node
# so the value is Desktop/rubix.
#
# Getting this wrong is the worst failure mode available here: the binary is
# copied somewhere systemd never reads, the service restarts happily on the
# OLD binary, and the summary still says OK. Always confirm afterwards with
#   cd .. && python3 node-versions.py
#
# Check a node's real path with:
#   ssh rubix@<host> 'systemctl cat rubixgoplatform | grep ExecStart'
REMOTE_BIN_REL=Desktop/rubix

# SSH user on the fleet.
SSH_USER=rubix

# Concurrent hosts. 0 = all at once (default). Set 1 to watch one at a time
# when chasing a failure.
JOBS=0


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Only for a fleet built by systems/install/setup.sh, which puts the binary at
# <clone>/nodes/<NODE_NAME>/. Ignored whenever REMOTE_BIN_REL is set above.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# REMOTE_REPO_REL=rubix-lab
# NODE_NAME=node
